/** Races & series. Motorsport and cycling, the sports /v2/sports marks with kind races, are organised in three levels. The smallest is the session: one timed part, which can be practice, qualifying, a sprint, the race itself or a stage of a cycling race. Sessions make up a race, which is a whole Grand Prix weekend or one cycling race, and races make up a series, the counterpart of a league elsewhere (Formula 1, MotoGP; in cycling, the complete men’s or women’s calendar). Live changes are pushed on the race:{id} WebSocket channel (Business plan and up); over REST the same three things, the race, its list of sessions and the results of one session, each have an endpoint of their own. Two conventions hold throughout: times are in milliseconds and distances in metres, and a driver, a rider or a team is a TeamRef, so /v2/teams/{id} returns its profile. */
